WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.467
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.200
It's an audience full

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.033
of veterans

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.033
-I know.
-and servicemen

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.067
-Thank you, guys.
-and -women.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:05.767
-Thank you.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.200
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.234
-You are -- You are Rambo.
You are Rambo.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:12.334
-Yeah, I'm pretend.
They're the real thing,

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.267
so, thank you very much, guys.
-Yeah.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:17.667
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:21.267
I'm sure, as being Rambo,
I'm sure a lot of veterans

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:23.567
have come to you
throughout the years.

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:25.133
-Yeah, they have.
They said like,

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.267
"You don't know
what you're doing."

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.667
"You cannot take on
half the world with a knife.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:31.667
It just doesn't work.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.701
[ Laughter ]
Or you cannot take a gun

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.701
that usually is mounted
on a helicopter,

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.234
hold it with one arm,
wrap bullets around your neck,

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:41.200
and just run
through the woods naked

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.667
[ Laughter ]
and actually
accomplish anything."

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.334
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:46.334
I don't know
if you remember this.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.167
The last time
we saw each other,

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:50.868
it was New Year's Eve
in Los Angeles, California.

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:52.701
-Oh, yeah.
It was a horrible day.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.467
[ Laughter ]
I remember.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:55.868
-It's not horrible.
-I know where you're going

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:56.801
with this.
-It was a great day.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:58.067
-Okay.
-It was one of my best --

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:00.667
It was one of the best memories
of my life.

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.334
I went to --
I was at the Polo Bar

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:04.067
-Right.
-at the Beverly Hills Hotel.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.367
-Right.
-There with my wife

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:06.767
-Right.
-and we're hanging out.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:09.267
We had a dinner
and it was New Year's

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:10.667
and they had a nice
piano player there.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.501
-Mm-hmm.
-And the piano player --

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.534
They said, "Jimmy, would you
like to sing something?"

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.234
-Right.
-And so I sang.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:17.367
I got up and sang
with the piano player.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:19.901
I sang "What Are You Doing
New Year's Eve?"

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.334
-Exactly.

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:23.067
[ Laughter ]
-And then I heard,

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:25.501
when I got done,
there was a round of applause

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:28.734
and someone said, "You have
the voice of an angel..."

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.000
-Mm-hmm.
-and gave me a $100 bill.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.701
-Yes.
-And that was you.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:32.767
-That was me.

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:35.801
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.868
That's only half the story.
-Yeah.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.934
-He got the money because I
wanted him to really shut up.

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:44.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.033
Giving me such a migraine,
guys, you know?

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.567
Christmas carols are rough,

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.133
but...
-Yeah, yeah, that one
was real bad.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.267
-Yeah.
It wasn't popular.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:54.300
It was like a weird song.
But go ahead.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.734
-I want to talk
about "Tulsa King,"

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:56.934
but before I do that...
-Yeah.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:58.701
-...you broke the Internet
a couple weeks ago

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.634
by posting this photo
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.234
-of you
and Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.534
carving pumpkins together.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.934
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh, my God.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.300
-Is this something you do?

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.934
-Well, usually,
we make pot holders,

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.934
[ Laughter ]
but this is, you know.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.601
Yeah, this is what happens
to get a little bit older.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:16.100
No, he --
I'm doing a reality show

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.501
and I gave him a call.
I says,

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:18.701
"Yeah, can I come over?"

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:20.400
He goes, "Yeah, come on over.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.400
I'll bring my donkey.
You can pet it."

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.334
[ Laughter ]
-"Come over and pet my donkey"?

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.601
-Pet my donkey.
Stroke my horse.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:28.968
I come over and there are these
fuzzy things in his office.

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:32.434
A donkey and a pony,
in the office!

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:35.701
I mean, not like,
okay, with diapers.
Just walking around.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.200
[ Laughter ]
I go, "When's it going
to take a dump?"

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.334
[ Laughter ]
I mean, who --

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:41.367
what secretary
signs up for that?

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.234
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.
-But, anyway,

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:48.167
after we do our little
tête-à-tête talking, he goes,

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.501
[ As Schwarzenegger ]
You want to carve a pumpkin?

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:52.367
[ Laughter ]
I go --

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:53.767
-[ As Schwarzenegger ]
You want to carve my pumpkin?

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.434
-I'm telling you.
-Yeah, I know, yeah.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:57.701
-And he goes like, "Pumpkin!"
And the pumpkins appear.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.234
Then it's like, "Knives!"

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:00.868
And some guy bringing knives.
I mean,

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:02.868
[ Laughter ]
it's unbelievably choreographed.

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:04.167
This guy's the real deal.
-I mean, these are crazy.

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:06.167
These aren't like
pumpkin carving knives.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.067
-No, when I saw this knife,
I go...

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:09.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.234
..."It's home team."

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.234
So, we had a pumpkin
carving contest

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:15.868
and I'm glad to say

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.467
that I went down,
got the head off,

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:18.868
both eyes and nose
and mouth done

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:20.100
before he got one eyeball.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.734
[ Cheering ]
-That's what I'm talking,
alright.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.701
That's what I'm talking about.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.300
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.701
Congrats on "Tulsa King."

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:28.267
-Thank you very much.
-You're getting rave reviews

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:29.501
on this already.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.067
I think it's perfect for you.

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:32.367
-Thank you.
-How would you describe

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:33.501
the character?

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:36.133
-Well, it's interesting
because it's --

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:37.801
it's very hard
to find a new concept,

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.267
but this is the guy
who takes a fall for someone,

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.868
who goes to jail for 25 years,
keeps his mouth shut,

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:45.968
expecting to be rewarded
by his Mafia "family."

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:49.367
Instead, he's shipped out
to Tulsa because they want

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:52.567
to get rid of him,
basically to drop dead and die.

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:55.067
And I thought, "Wow, this is all
about loneliness

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.901
and starting over,"
because the worst thing

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:59.267
that could ever happen
to anybody is like

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:01.901
drop your life and, literally,
you are shipped out somewhere.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.100
You go, "How do I start over?

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.868
I'm like 76 years old."

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.334
But that's the beauty.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:09.000
He starts a new family there,
but there's no Italians,

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.133
there's no Mafia guys,

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:13.300
so, I'm getting like
computer nerds, cowboys,

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:17.467
Indian guys, you know, I mean,
really, the most oddball group

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:20.334
and that becomes my new,
weird gang family.

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:22.467
-Yeah.
-So, it provides a lot of comedy

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.133
and it's interesting.

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:25.868
And I do go Rambo a couple
of times.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:26.934
[ Cheering and applause ]
No, he does --

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:28.767
He does, I mean --

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:32.000
-Yeah, you do.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.567
In the first three minutes
of what I saw,

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.534
I think you knocked out
like five guys.

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:37.367
-Yes.
-Yeah, but, I mean, but, yeah.

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:38.934
But you -
It is very funny, by the way.

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:40.534
-But they deserved it!
-Yeah.

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:41.601
[ Laughter ]
Of course!

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:43.033
Of course they deserved it,
yeah.

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:47.033
I saw you showed Demi Lovato how
to do an onscreen fight scene.

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:48.167
-Yeah, that's right.

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:49.467
-Take a look at this thing.
Watch this.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.200
-Jab me.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.067
[ Clunk ]

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:52.801
-Go get him, D!

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.067
[ Clunk ]

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:56.000
[Indistinct].

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.133
[ Clunking ]

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:58.501
Okay. Here it comes.

00:04:58.501 --> 00:04:59.501
Here it comes.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:00.434
Unh!

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:01.133
[ Clunk ]

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.601
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:05.934
-Demi -- Demi Lovato!

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:10.834
-Now, you don't, for a second,
think that's real.

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:12.000
That was an art form.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.000
That shows you how you
can actually choreograph

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.033
and fake a punch,

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.634
but it takes
a little bit of practice,

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.067
and I don't know if you got it.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:21.067
[ Oohs, cheering, and applause ]
I mean, you know.

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:22.601
I don't know.

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:23.467
I don't know.

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:24.868
I think Demi could take you out.

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:26.267
That's -- I'm just saying.

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.100
-You don't think I could
take a fake punch?

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.000
-I don't you could take
a fake punch.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.133
-[ As Schwarzenegger ]
You want to carve my pumpkin?

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:33.901
What are you doing?

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:35.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.701
You know,
you can't take my punch.

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.767
You can't take my fake punch.
How's that?

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:41.067
-Can you give me a tip on how I
could take a fake punch?

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:42.300
-You actually want to do this?

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.234
-I would love -- Yeah.

00:05:43.234 --> 00:05:45.901
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.167
[ Whistling ]

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:49.200
-You tell me where to stand.
-Alright.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.234
Alright, what do I do?

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:51.467
I'm getting nervous.
-I'm serious.

00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:52.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:53.467
This is making me so nervous.

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:55.100
-Oh, no, no, no, seriously.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.934
Alright, now, first of all --
-Okay.

00:05:57.934 --> 00:06:00.567
-Well, you got to put
a little water in your mouth

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:02.968
because what I'm going to do is
I'm going to lay it on you.

00:06:02.968 --> 00:06:05.100
If you get close,
I will break your jaw.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.567
I mean, I'm just telling you
right now.

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:08.033
I don't want to hurt you.
I like you.

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.667
You're tall, good-looking.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.000
[ Laughter ]
But,

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.200
you're now --
-Stop, stop, stop, stop,
stop, aah!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.467
[ Laughter ]
Ow, ow, ow! Ow!

00:06:14.467 --> 00:06:15.667
This is what I said to De Niro.

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:17.901
We were doing "Grudge Match"
together. I go,

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:20.000
"Those damn Oscars ain't gonna
save you in here."

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:20.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.968
Okay, so.

00:06:22.968 --> 00:06:24.167
-A sip of water?
-Water in there

00:06:24.167 --> 00:06:25.634
-Okay.
-and then I'm going to throw

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:27.968
-Uh-huh.
-like wham! A left.

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:30.667
And you're going to do a spin
and spit the water out

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:32.434
and make it look like
you're really in trouble.

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:33.501
-Okay.

00:06:33.501 --> 00:06:35.067
[ Cheering and applause ]
I'm so scared.

00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:39.167
[ Mumbling ]

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:41.534
-Right?

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:42.234
Huah!

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:45.767
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:45.767 --> 00:06:46.834
[ Whistling ]

00:06:46.834 --> 00:06:48.334
-It was good?
-That was good.

00:06:48.334 --> 00:06:49.601
-Slow motion, can we see?

00:06:51.467 --> 00:06:53.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:57.801
I want to show another clip.

00:06:57.801 --> 00:06:59.901
Here's Sylvester Stallone
in "Tulsa King."

00:06:59.901 --> 00:07:01.501
Take a look at this.

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.934
-It seems we have
a slight misunderstanding.

00:07:03.934 --> 00:07:05.934
See, my associate was
in earlier,

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:09.767
trying to buy that Navigator
that you got downstairs,

00:07:09.767 --> 00:07:11.634
but you wouldn't sell it to him.

00:07:11.634 --> 00:07:13.834
-Oh, boy.
I-I'm so sorry.

00:07:13.834 --> 00:07:15.868
-Why, Donnie?

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.567
Well, you know, it was
a total misunderstanding,

00:07:17.567 --> 00:07:19.567
like you said yourself.

00:07:19.567 --> 00:07:22.334
-The truth is, he's a good kid.

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:24.767
Probably never had
a day of trouble in his life.

00:07:24.767 --> 00:07:28.000
You know, see, the problem is,
you see a young Black guy

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.934
with a mountain of money
and, right away, you say,

00:07:29.934 --> 00:07:31.968
"Hey, he's got to be
a drug dealer."

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:35.767
-Oh!
-But I walk in, in a nice suit,

00:07:35.767 --> 00:07:38.434
and you're not afraid anymore.

00:07:38.434 --> 00:07:40.934
See, the irony is

00:07:40.934 --> 00:07:42.501
he's afraid of the wrong thing.

00:07:44.334 --> 00:07:45.501
-I'm not following.

00:07:45.501 --> 00:07:46.868
-Well, follow this.

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:48.834
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah!

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:51.100
[ Thud ]
Exactly right!

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:52.000
[ Whistling ]

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.601
Sylvester Stallone, everybody.

00:07:53.601 --> 00:07:58.067
"Tulsa King" premieres Sunday,
exclusively on Paramount+.

00:07:58.067 --> 00:07:59.734
We'll be right back
with Linda Cardellini.

00:07:59.734 --> 00:08:01.200
Stick around.
Do one more?

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.601
[ Funk plays ]

00:08:02.601 --> 00:08:05.100
-♪ Let's see if I was real,
unh ♪

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.534
♪ Try to see if God is real ♪

00:08:06.534 --> 00:08:10.801
♪♪

